@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 24
skinparam ranksep 40
title Money UC04 / UC05 - focused design - REVIEW
class MoneyController {
  +credit(accountId: UUID, dto: CreditRequest): OperationResult
  +debit(accountId: UUID, dto: DebitRequest): OperationResult
 }
class MoneyService {
  +credit(claim: Claim, account: UUID, amount: long): FinancialResult
  +consume(claim: Claim, cycle: UUID, account: UUID, amount: long): FinancialResult
 }
class OperationCoordinator {
  +claim(caller: Caller, op: Operation, id: String, canonical: Bytes): Claim
  +lookup(caller: Caller, op: Operation, id: String): OperationResult
  +recoverProcessing(batch: int): int
 }
interface OperationRequestStore {
  +insertClaim(key: RequestKey, hash: String): Claim
  +lockWithFence(id: UUID, fence: long): OperationRequest
  +storeTerminal(result: OperationResult): void
 }
class MoneyCore {
  +checkEligibilityLocked(account: Account, now: Instant): Eligibility
  +applyLocked(account: Account, delta: long, eligibility: Eligibility): BalanceChange
 }
interface AccountStore {
  +lock(accountId: UUID): Account
  +updateBalance(change: BalanceChange): void
 }
interface LedgerStore {
  +append(entry: FinancialEntry): UUID
 }
interface SubscriptionStore {
  +ensureEmptyGuard(subscriber: UUID, packageId: UUID): UUID
  +lock(root: UUID): Subscription
  +insertCycle(cycle: PaidCycle): void
  +incrementVersion(root: Subscription): void
 }
interface DbClock {
  +nowUtcAfterLock(): Instant
 }
interface TransactionBoundary {
  +readCommitted(work: Work): Result
  +rollbackAndRetryTransient(work: Work): Result
 }
MoneyController --> MoneyService
MoneyService --> OperationCoordinator
OperationCoordinator --> OperationRequestStore
MoneyService --> MoneyCore
MoneyCore --> AccountStore
MoneyCore --> DbClock
MoneyService --> LedgerStore
MoneyService --> SubscriptionStore : consumption cycle
MoneyService ..> TransactionBoundary : one RC transaction
note bottom of MoneyCore
  Lock account, root and cycle first.
  Sample fresh DB time immediately before writes.
  Balance + ledger + terminal result commit together.
  No fallback; FAILED is final; unknown COMMIT requires lookup.
end note
legend bottom
  Focused view: selected classes from backend-design-class.puml.
  Cross-cutting access checks / operation coordination remain in full overview.
  Methods show responsibilities and ports, not JPA entities.
endlegend
@enduml
